[# docs-src/repos/cx-platform-xsp.cxd — the stream protocol's page,
   repo-cx-platform-xsp.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 3).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from its own corpus (the xsp
   suite). #]

[repo name=cx-platform-xsp
  [intro
    """One frame, any transport, and a handshake whose every verb is
       pure. `cx-platform-xsp` is the XAP Stream Protocol: a
       self-describing, self-delimiting frame — version, type, stream,
       principal, flags, length, payload — that carries the platform's
       traffic over whatever socket is underneath, and XSP-AUTH, the mutual
       proof-of-control handshake the store, identity and the fabric open
       their connections with."""]
  [body
    """The codec is two pure verbs. `encode` turns a `[frame]` element into
       bytes and `decode` reads one back, reporting how many bytes it
       consumed so a reader can step to the next frame; `decode-all` walks a
       buffer and hands back the trailing partial frame as a value rather
       than losing it. A binary payload carries a CX element losslessly —
       attributes, children, text, an empty element — because a transport
       whose users have to know which values survive the trip is not a
       transport. Every way a frame can be wrong has its own refusal: a reserved
       flag, a foreign version, a truncated header, a length past the
       declared ceiling."""]
  [body
    """XSP-AUTH is four messages on stream 0, signed ephemeral X25519 in the
       SIGMA shape, with a per-request possession proof and a rotation
       continuity proof beside it. Its verbs take their randomness as an
       argument and answer values, so the whole handshake is graded in the
       corpus without a socket, and credit frames carry the flow control a
       stream negotiates. The protocol pages themselves live in this
       repository's spec directory below."""]
  [gives
    """Two modules: the frame codec, a Ring 1 module under the `cx-stdlib`
       namespace because it is pure and reaches nothing, and the handshake
       calculus in the platform group. Each links to the reference page
       projected from its own documentation."""]
  [try
    """Every frame type the protocol defines, encoded and decoded in turn, the
       type read back from the frame — eight round trips, no grant, no
       socket."""]
  [fixture id=xsp-002-roundtrip-all-eight-types]
  [status
    """The stream protocol builds on the language alone and is built on by
       the store, identity, the fabric and the application host, which reach
       the handshake calculus through the pin; the front door compiles its V
       module from the same pin."""]]
